    IDT_SEC_WORLD   = "World",
    IDT_SEC_COLLECTIONS = "Collections",
    QOL_NAV_SOLORAIDFRAME = "Solo Raid Frame",
    QOL_ABOUT_SOLORAIDFRAME = "Keeps the game's raid-style party frame shown while you are not in a group, so your own frame is there when you play solo too (Edit Mode: Party Frames, Use Raid-Style Party Frames). In a group, the game's own rule. When a group ends (someone leaving, an invitation declined), it comes back at once, in combat too (through the game's own secure state driver). No settings.",
    QOL_NAV_ENHANCEDRAIDFRAMES = "Enhanced Raid Frames",
    QOL_ABOUT_ENHANCEDRAIDFRAMES = "On the game's raid frames (and raid-style party frames): up to nine indicators per frame, each showing the auras you list (by name, spell ID, or debuff type: Magic, Curse, Poison, Disease, Dispel), as an icon or a colored square, with time left, stacks and colors; raid target markers; the frames' scale, background opacity and out-of-range opacity. Converted for WoW Forever: in combat the game itself shows the buffs and the debuff types you list. Command: /erf.",
    ERF_SW_MARKERS  = "Raid target markers on the frames",
    QOL_NAV_DOESITDIE = "DoesItDie",
    QOL_ABOUT_DOESITDIE = "Your DoTs on the target: the damage they still have to deal is marked on its health bar (and on the focus's and the nameplates'), with a kill icon on the portrait when they will finish it off. Made for WoW Forever: the comparison with its secret health is done by the game's own bars. By default in the game's look (the health bar's own texture, a dark red, the game's boss skull); the options window has a live preview and DoesItDie's other looks. Command: /did.",
    QOL_NAV_LFGFOREVER = "LFG Forever",
    QOL_ABOUT_LFGFOREVER = "The game's group finder in one window: groups and players in one list, filtered by role, class, level, playstyle and language, with Ask to Join and Invite that whisper your message, a log of the whispers you get and saved filters. The filters' panel on the right closes with the arrow at the top right of the list (closed until you open it), with a Search Again button beside it. Command: /lfg, or its key, its minimap button, or its tab on the game's group finder.",
    LFGFOREVER_BINDING = "Open LFG Forever",
    QOL_NAV_WHATSTRAINING = "What's Training?",
    QOL_ABOUT_WHATSTRAINING = "What your class trainer (and the weapon masters, the pet trainer, the tomes) can teach you, now and at the next levels, with its cost, and the recipes your professions can still learn and where. In Forever's spellbook: a tab of its own, on the book's own pages; with ClassicUI's spellbook: its \"What can I train?\" side tab opens the classic list beside the book. Command: /wt (its window).",
    QOL_NAV_ENEMYCASTS = "Enemy Casts",
    QOL_ABOUT_ENEMYCASTS = "Beside an enemy's nameplate, what it just did: the spell it casts (its icon, its name under it), held while the cast lasts and tinted red when it is interrupted, and the instant spells it uses. The last few stay in a row, the newest by the plate, each fading after a moment. Left or right of the plate, or above it; the icons' size, how many stay and for how long are on its page (Esc > Options > AddOns > Clara > Combat > Enemy Casts). Made for WoW Forever: a secret spell is never read, the game draws it itself. Clara's own (not ForeverGCD's code).",
    EC_CASTS        = "Spells being cast",
