    -- page in the game's options (Esc > Options > AddOns)
    SP_RESET_POS    = "Bring the options window back",
    SP_OPEN         = "Open the options (/cl)",
    SP_LOCK_ALL     = "Lock everything",
    SP_UNLOCK       = "Unlock the bar",
    SP_RESET_ADDON  = "Reset the addon...",
    SP_WINDOW_SIZE  = "Options window size",
    SP_DEFAULT_SIZE = "Default size",
    SP_HINT         = "The options window moves by its title, even off the screen, and gets bigger or smaller from its bottom right corner. /cl reset pos also brings it back.",
    SP_HOW          = "How it works",
    SP_README       = "|cffffd200What the addon does|r\nA bar for every class: combo points (rogues, druids), energy or rage (rogues, druids, warriors), mana, health, and up to three rows of icons above and below it to follow buffs, debuffs and cooldowns. Druids see combo points and energy / rage in Cat and Bear Form (can be changed).\n\n|cffffd200The options|r\n/cl (or /clara, /ccp, /cp) opens the window on the tab and page shown last (the first time, your class's tab). Each class tab has its own settings, on five pages listed on the left: General (size, opacity, style and text of the bars), Bars (order, size and colors of each bar), Icons, Visibility (showing or hiding the addon, druid forms, the portrait's menu) and Profiles. Drag a page in the list to change its place; right-click the portrait to give the tab a specialization's icon. The window moves by its title, even off the screen. Its bottom right corner sizes it: hold the left mouse button and drag to change its width and height (the pages scroll when it is shorter than them), the right button to make it bigger or smaller, double-click to get the default size back. Its opacity is set at the bottom right.\n\n|cffffd200Opacity and hiding|r\nRight-click your portrait: at the end of the menu (the game lets addons add only after its own entries; not in combat), the Clara Combo Points section has Reload UI, a slider for the bar's opacity followed by two boxes: bar and icons locked for every class, then show / hide the whole addon (also /cl hide and /cl show); under them, Show damage meter, and Dynamic camera (DynamicCam's Vertical Pitch and Head Tracking on or off, your Zoom Increments for each), then Fishing mode (music, ambience and voices off, sound effects at 100 %, to hear the bobber; also on the Fishing card of the professions window, and above with how much louder). Both this section and Reload UI can be left out of the menu above.\n\n|cffffd200Moving the bar|r\nPosition (above the class tabs) > Unlock, then drag the bar with the left mouse button. Its icon rows open too, for every class: drop spells from the spellbook or items from your bags on them, drag the icons, right-click one to remove it. Lock it afterwards (the button, /cl lock, or Lock everything above).\n\n|cffffd200Icons|r\nIcons page: type a spell name or ID, drag a spell from the spellbook onto a row, or open Class spells to pick a buff or debuff of any class, a spell of the General tab or of a race, with its rank and where to watch it (Show only known spells keeps those of your spellbook; its lock detaches that panel to move and size it on its own, locking it again puts it back on the side of the window it is on). A spell on the cursor (from the spellbook, the chat or an action bar) or dragged from that panel opens the rows of the bar itself, even locked: drop it on one. Click an icon to watch it on you, your target, an enemy target or a friendly target, to pick its rank or to remove it. Right-click it, or drag it out of the window, to remove it. With the icons locked, a click on an icon of the bar casts its spell when your character knows it; a spell that needs a form or a stance (Maul, Charge...) takes that form first, and a second click casts it; Feral Charge: left click Bear Form, right click Cat Form. A spell just learned can be taken from its line in the chat (press on its name). A grayed out icon waits for its aura; the swipe and the countdown show how long it lasts; a spell with a cooldown shows its cooldown.\n\n|cffffd200Items and weapon imbues|r\nAn icon can be an item: drag it from your bags (bar unlocked). It shows how many you carry, its cooldown and its buff; a click uses it. Poisons, oils and stones show your weapon's enchantment (left-click: main hand, right-click: off hand). The shaman's weapon imbues show the time left on the weapon; Windfury Weapon shows its 1.5 second internal cooldown after an extra attack. While a spell with a cast time is cast, the mana it costs is marked on the mana bar.\n\n|cffffd200In combat|r\nThe game hides auras from addons during combat. It shows them itself in its aura containers: buffs on you or a friendly target and debuffs on an enemy target stay followed. A debuff on you or a buff on an enemy is only followed out of combat. If an icon stays gray in combat, type /cl debug and send what it prints.\n\n|cffffd200Profiles|r\nProfiles page: type a name, then Save, to keep all the settings of the tab. Pick a profile in the list to Load or Delete it. Export gives a text to copy; on another account, use Import and paste it. Before another profile is loaded, the addon offers to save the changes not saved yet. Tick Load it in my specialization when saving: that profile then loads by itself whenever your character is in that specialization.\n\n|cffffd200Built-in modules|r\nOther addons' features are built in (WoW Forever only), under this page by theme: Combat, Interface, Quests and progress, Economy and professions; each module with its box, what it does, and its own pages under its theme. The bar's own options are on the first page (Clara Combo Points), or in their window (/clara). When a module's own addon is enabled, that one runs for the session, then it is turned off for the character and the built-in one takes over from the next reload (its settings carried over).\n\n|cffffd200/who|r\n/who lea lists every name with lea in it, as the game does (Leah, Leafrunner...). /who \"lea\" (one word in quotes) lists only the players whose first name or surname is Lea, accents aside (Léa, Lëa; not Leah). A box above turns it off.\n\n|cffffd200UnitScan|r\nAn alert as soon as one of WoW Forever's rares, a name you add or the hunted mob is in sight (your target, the mouseover, the nameplates, your group's targets): a window to click to target it, a sound, the screen flashing, the game's icon flashing in the taskbar while you are in another window. UnitScan Hardcore Forever's sightings are always received; yours are sent only if you tick the box (off). Esc > Options > AddOns > Clara > Quests and progress > UnitScan, or /cl scan. Screenshots: at each level gained and at the first kill of each boss (raids, dungeons 54+, a leveling dungeon's last boss), per character.\n\n|cffffd200Commands|r\n/cl lock  ·  /cl unlock  ·  /cl hide  ·  /cl show  ·  /cl scale 120 (bar size, in %)  ·  /cl reset (everything back to the defaults, after a confirmation)  ·  /cl reset pos (options window back in the middle of the screen)  ·  /cl debug (state of the icons)  ·  /cl help  ·  /cl scan (UnitScan; /cl scan Name: a name added or removed)  ·  /cl hunt Name (the hunted mob)  ·  /rl (reload the interface)  ·  /ltp (Leatrix Plus)  ·  /wst (WeaponSwingTimer)  ·  /dc (DynamicCam)  ·  /dk (DialogKey)  ·  /xtl (XToLevel)  ·  /mmd (MinimapDrawer)  ·  /fcui (ClassicUI Forever)  ·  /buyemall confirm",
  },
